meta {
  name: ENG - list EC classes
  type: http
  seq: 27
}

get {
  url: {{engBaseUrl}}/api/classes
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  x-functions-key: {{engFunctionKey}}
}

docs {
  The class catalog the ENG panel's ECCLASS dropdown is populated from, read
  straight from EngProvider rather than through the Sandbox.

  The key travels as a header, not as a `code=` query parameter. Both authenticate,
  but the provider's own routes read `code` as a filter — GetTags does exactly that —
  so a key in that position is ambiguous at best and silently filters at worst.
  It also keeps the secret out of the URL, and out of this file: set engBaseUrl and
  engFunctionKey in an environment, which is where values that must not be committed
  belong.
}
